# Cursor AI Configuration

## Project Context
React 19 frontend application in cross-repository environment with backend service. Team of 3 co-located developers using comprehensive AI development workflows.

## Core Guidelines
- Modern React 19 patterns with functional components and hooks
- Cross-repository integration with backend service
- Comprehensive testing with Jest and React Testing Library
- AI-assisted development, code review, and testing workflows

## Documentation References
- Central Context: `docs/central-context.md`
- React Patterns: `docs/react-development-guide.md`
- Code Review: `docs/code-review-standards.md`
- Testing: `docs/testing-guidelines.md`

## Code Generation Rules
- Use React 19 functional components with hooks
- Implement proper TypeScript/JavaScript patterns
- Generate comprehensive tests alongside code
- Follow accessibility best practices
- Include error handling and loading states

## Quality Standards
- Clean, readable, maintainable code
- Performance-optimized patterns
- Cross-repository consistency
- Comprehensive documentation
- Thorough test coverage

## Team Workflow
- Support 3-developer co-located team
- Enable cross-repository context sharing
- Facilitate code review and testing processes
- Maintain documentation consistency

## Integration Focus
- Backend API integration patterns
- Shared data model consistency
- Error handling across repositories
- End-to-end workflow support
